gridcoinresearch (5.5.2.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  The testnet daemon's systemd units are new in this release, and the system
  service was switched over to them during this upgrade. This is what changed.

  gridcointestnetd.service runs as the account gridcointestnet. systemd hands
  /var/lib/gridcointestnetd to the new account at the service's first start,
  and /etc/gridcoin-testnet is now root:gridcointestnet 0710. A
  /etc/gridcoin-testnet/gridcoin.conf owned by root is given the group
  gridcointestnet and made readable by that group only; one owned by gridcoin
  must be given to root:gridcointestnet, mode 0640, by hand. A missing one is
  created as root:gridcointestnet 0640 with generated RPC credentials.

  The unit is Type=notify: the core reports to systemd itself when it is
  ready, with no forking and no pid file. It passes -nodaemon and
  -nodaemonwait, so daemon=1 or daemonwait=1 in a configuration file no longer
  matters.

  Overrides written for the old forking unit would make the new one fail at
  every start, so they were moved aside. A drop-in in
  /etc/systemd/system/gridcointestnetd.service.d that sets ExecStart=, Type=,
  PIDFile=, NotifyAccess=, User= (User=gridcoin, say) or Group= was renamed to
  <name>.disabled-by-gridcoin-switchover, and so was a copy of the unit at
  /etc/systemd/system/gridcointestnetd.service. The upgrade named each one.
  Review them, and put back with "systemctl edit" what still applies. A mask
  was left as it was.

  A desktop user attaches the GUI to the system service through membership of
  the gridcointestnet-gui group ("Connect to the system service" in the
  menu). A new membership takes effect at the user's next login.

  The package also has a per-user unit, gridcointestnetd@<user>.service, which
  runs the core as that user. Set it up with
  "gridcointestnet-service enable-user <user>": "systemctl enable" alone gives
  an instance that stops with exit status 78 and says so. A per-user core and
  the system service conflict, and one stops the other. Hosts that ran a test
  build with per-user units had them switched over too, with the datadir they
  used, unless the system service was enabled or running.

  If the switch-over did not finish, the upgrade said why, and
  /var/lib/gridcoin-service/switchover-test.state keeps what is left. Fix the
  cause and run "gridcointestnet-service switch-over
  --state=/var/lib/gridcoin-service/switchover-test.state". Until then a core
  it left is not restarted, and once stopped it may not start again.

  The full description:
  https://github.com/gridcoin-community/Gridcoin-Research/blob/development/doc/running-unattended.md

 -- Gridcoin Developers <dev@gridcoin.us>  Thu, 05 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
